  data: {
    LLM: "Try to hold two strong suits which total to seven, such as 2s and 5s. This gives you multiple playing options on different end values.\n\nThe blanks (0s) are important - they can force opponents to use matadors or block one end of the train. The 0-0 is the most valuable tile since it guarantees a play and can block an end.\n\nSave matadors to change the end of the train to a value you can match, or to block an opponent who doesn't have matadors. If the train ends in 4 and you play the 3-4 matador with the 4 touching the train, the new end is 4; if you play it with the 3 touching, the new end is 3 - choose based on your hand and opponent needs.",
    Player: "Try to hold two strong suits which total to seven, such as 2s and 5s. This gives you multiple playing options on different end values.\n\nThe blanks (0s) are important - they can force opponents to use matadors or block one end of the train. The 0-0 is the most valuable tile since it guarantees a play and can block an end.\n\nSave matadors to change the end of the train to a value you can match, or to block an opponent who doesn't have matadors. If the train ends in 4 and you play the 3-4 matador with the 4 touching the train, the new end is 4; if you play it with the 3 touching, the new end is 3 - choose based on your hand and opponent needs.",
